From 86dda88847fb5c10ce13df0734102ec73bcd3608 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: William Emerison Six <billsix@gmail.com>
Date: Tue, 22 Sep 2026 16:38:35 +0000
Subject: [PATCH 16/36] code, overlays/actors: delete the self-assignments and
 the lone `;` kept "to match"
MIME-Version: 1.0
Content-Type: text/plain; charset=UTF-8
Content-Transfer-Encoding: 8bit

`sp30 = sp30;`, `pos = pos;`, `spE8 = spE8;`, `normalVec = normalVec;`
(z_eff_blure.c, Bg_Hidan_Hamstep, Mir_Ray) and the empty statement after
Audio_SetSequenceMode in code_800EC960.c. Each existed only to shape the
ROM's stack frame or register allocation. (The pointer-spelled twin in
En_Ma3 is NOT a no-op in the generated code — the store back through
the pointer survives — so it is left for the explained-diff list.)

Verified: every file compiles to byte-identical assembly before and
after with the port's own flags (asmdiff over compile_commands.json).

Co-Authored-By: Claude Fable 5.1 <noreply@anthropic.com>
---
 soh/src/code/code_800EC960.c                                  | 1 -
 soh/src/code/z_eff_blure.c                                    | 2 --
 .../overlays/actors/ovl_Bg_Hidan_Hamstep/z_bg_hidan_hamstep.c | 1 -
 soh/src/overlays/actors/ovl_Mir_Ray/z_mir_ray.c               | 4 ----
 4 files changed, 8 deletions(-)

diff --git a/soh/src/code/code_800EC960.c b/soh/src/code/code_800EC960.c
index 1cc4dbf44..e5cd54cef 100644
--- a/soh/src/code/code_800EC960.c
+++ b/soh/src/code/code_800EC960.c
@@ -3695,7 +3695,6 @@ void AudioDebug_ProcessInput_BlkChgBgm(void) {
         sAudioBlkChgBgmWork[sAudioBlkChgBgmSel]--;
         if (sAudioBlkChgBgmSel == 1) {
             Audio_SetSequenceMode(sAudioBlkChgBgmWork[1]);
-            ; // might be a fake match?
         }
     }
 
diff --git a/soh/src/code/z_eff_blure.c b/soh/src/code/z_eff_blure.c
index 56e595149..bd861fef8 100644
--- a/soh/src/code/z_eff_blure.c
+++ b/soh/src/code/z_eff_blure.c
@@ -490,8 +490,6 @@ void EffectBlure_GetComputedValues(EffectBlure* this, s32 index, f32 ratio, Vec3
             break;
     }
 
-    sp30 = sp30; // Optimized out but seems necessary to match stack usage
-
     if (this->flags & 0x10) {
         color1->r = color1->g = color1->b = color1->a = 255;
         color2->r = color2->g = color2->b = color2->a = 255;
diff --git a/soh/src/overlays/actors/ovl_Bg_Hidan_Hamstep/z_bg_hidan_hamstep.c b/soh/src/overlays/actors/ovl_Bg_Hidan_Hamstep/z_bg_hidan_hamstep.c
